<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq-section" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header r-left">
      <div class="tag">Common Questions</div>
      <h2>Before you call,<br>read this.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>Do you work weekends and evenings to meet tight deadlines?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. We build shift flexibility into every project plan upfront. Weekend pushes and extended hours are standard practice at VNG, not an exception that requires a change order. When you're falling behind, the answer is more crew — not a timeline extension.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>How do you handle scope changes mid-project?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>With a written change order, a revised timeline impact, and a clear cost before any work changes. No verbal agreements. No surprises on the final invoice. If you authorize it in writing, you know what it costs and what it does to the schedule before we start.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>Do you self-perform all trades or subcontract?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We self-perform demolition, framing, drywall, and finishing. Mechanical, electrical, and plumbing are coordinated through vetted trade partners we have worked with for years. These aren't random subs — they're trades who know our standards and our schedules.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>What size of project is VNG built for?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We are most effective on projects between $50K and $2M in construction value. Large enough to need real coordination and trade management, scoped enough that you still get our full attention. Outside that range, we will tell you honestly whether we are the right fit.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>Are you insured and WSIB compliant?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Full general liability insurance, WSIB clearance in good standing, and complete documentation available on request — before contract signing, not after. We do not start work without your compliance requirements satisfied.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

